  "transcript": "I find a chair for $9. It has four legs a seat and the confidence of a much better chair, so he buys it. For the first week, everything is fine, then the chair starts making a noise that sounds like legal advice. The screw gets loose. One leg begins exploring other career options, and suddenly the cheap chair was not really cheap. It was a normal chair with one small problem, future not included. So next time something looks cheap. The better question is not, how much does it cost? It is how much future is included.",
